# health v2.8 — WARNING. A lab result status outside Observation.status.
#
# "completed" is a real FHIR code on workflow resources and is in no
# Observation.status value set. It is what a converter writes when it maps a
# general "this finished" state onto a result.
#
# What is lost when this is unchecked is specific, and health.shapes.ttl states
# it: "amended" and "corrected" are what distinguish a superseded result from
# the one that replaced it. A status carrier that accepts any string cannot make
# that distinction, and no reader downstream can restore it.
#
# sh:Warning per the core v3.5 ratchet -- existing pods carry this predicate and
# v1.5 of these shapes is the first release to bind its value -- so the fixture
# asserts that the value is REPORTED and that the record is NOT rejected. See
# fixtures/clinical/status-vitalsign-completed.WARN.ttl for why a two-polarity
# filename cannot state that.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:uuid:1ab00208-0000-4000-8000-000000000002> a health:LabResultRecord ;
    health:testName "Hemoglobin A1c" ;
    health:testCode "4548-4" ;
    health:resultValue "6.8" ;
    health:resultUnit "%" ;
    health:performedDate "2031-04-18"^^xsd:date ;
    clinical:status "completed" ;
    clinical:sourceEHR "Meridian Health System" ;
    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified ;
    cascade:schemaVersion "1.4" .
